  TextBox - Advanced text container with editing capabilities

  - Purpose: Complex text container for large/editable content
  - Content handling: Uses TextBuffer - a sophisticated text management system
  - Size: Fixed size container that can hold more content than fits
  - Scrolling: Full scrolling support (scrollX, scrollY, scroll bars, etc.)
  - Text handling: Advanced - word wrap, line wrap, tab handling, cursor management
  - Text editing: Supports text editing, selection, clipboard operations
  - Use case: Text editors, logs, large text content, scrollable text areas

  Key architectural difference:

  - Text: Renders text directly to the output - think <span> or <p>
  - TextBox: Contains a TextBuffer which manages text separately from display - think <textarea> or text editor

  So Text is for simple static text display, while TextBox is a full-featured text container/editor with scrolling and advanced
  text management. That's why TextBox has its own scrolling implementation - it needs specialized text-aware scrolling behavior
