  Yoga's Limitations for Inline Layout

  Yoga does NOT support inline-flex or inline layout. Here's why:

  What Yoga Does Support:

  - Block-level Flexbox: Standard flex containers (display: flex)
  - Flex properties: flex-direction, justify-content, align-items, etc.
  - Box model: padding, margins, borders, absolute positioning

  What Yoga Does NOT Support:

  - display: inline - No inline layout mode
  - display: inline-flex - No inline flex containers
  - Text wrapping - No text flow or line breaking
  - Mixed content layout - Can't mix text and elements in flowing lines

  The Open GitHub Issue

  There's an open issue (#968) requesting display: inline-block support, which confirms that Yoga
   currently only handles block-level layout.

  Implications for TOM

  This means we can't use Yoga for inline text layout. We'd need:

  1. Yoga for block layout - containers, buttons, structured UI
  2. Custom inline engine - for text flow, wrapping, mixed styling

  Alternative Approach

  Instead of trying to make Yoga do inline layout, we could:

  // Block containers use Yoga
  <container style={{display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column'}}>

    // Text containers use custom inline layout
    <text-flow>
      <text-node>Hello </text-node>
      <text style={{fontWeight: 'bold'}}>bold</text>
      <text-node> world!</text-node>
    </text-flow>

  </container>

  So the plan would be:
  - Keep Yoga for structural layout (containers, buttons, grids)
  - Build custom inline engine for rich text within text containers
  - Hybrid approach - best of both worlds

  This actually makes the architecture cleaner - block layout and inline layout are fundamentally
   different problems that need different solutions.


